To optimize performance during the simulation, we precompute mappings between HUD factors (brightness, information frequency, FoV, and information relevance) and their effects on driver states (awareness, distraction, and fatigue). The Appendix details and visualizes these mappings derived from empirical studies and established relationships in the literature (see Table I, Table II, and Table III).
At the beginning of the simulation, we initialize the driver state for each vehicle, setting base values for awareness, distraction, and fatigue levels as specified in Table III. Vehicles are then assigned HUD configurations based on predefined probabilities, allowing us to simulate a variety of HUD settings within the same traffic environment.
The Appendix shows that HUD factors do not always influence the driving performance directly but influence the driver states: awareness, distraction, and fatigue level, affecting the driving performance (see Table III).

